%
% HOW BIBTEX WORKS (quick primer):
% ---------------------------------
% 1. This file lives in the same directory as thesis.tex.
%    The line \bibliography{thesis} in thesis.tex tells LaTeX
%    to look for a file named "thesis.bib".
%
% 2. Each entry below has the form:
%       @TYPE{citekey,
%         field1 = {value},
%         field2 = {value},
%       }
%    where TYPE is article, book, inproceedings, misc, etc.
%    and citekey is the short label you use in your .tex files,
%    e.g. \citep{tibshirani1996lasso} or \citet{carvalho2010horseshoe}.
%
% 3. To cite a reference in your text:
%       \citep{citekey}   --> (Author, Year)   [parenthetical]
%       \citet{citekey}   --> Author (Year)     [textual]
%    These commands come from the natbib package loaded in thesis.tex.
%
% 4. Compilation order (run these in sequence, or let Overleaf do it):
%       pdflatex thesis
%       bibtex   thesis
%       pdflatex thesis
%       pdflatex thesis
%    The first pdflatex pass writes thesis.aux; bibtex reads it and
%    writes thesis.bbl; the final two passes embed the bibliography
%    and resolve all citation cross-references.
%
% 5. Only entries that are actually cited in the document will appear
%    in the printed bibliography -- unused entries are ignored.
%
% =============================================================================

